speechtext:
They might do what
persons who commit a'ssaults very often do;

they go before a friendly magistrate very quickly, plead guilty and pay a small fine before the real complainant can get at them. If a distiller in Ontario, or in the upper provinces-because that is where the distilleries are; we have none in the lower provinces-was guilty of violating the law by sending liquor to Prince Edward Island, before the zealous temperance people there, like my hon. friend from Kings (Mir. Hughes), could get at that distiller down in the island, the distiller might go before a friendly magistrate in Ontario, plead guilty of the offence, be convicted, and that would bar proceedings in Prince Edward Island.
